# open-claude-gpt configuration — copy to .env and `source` it, or export in your shell.
# Every value has a working default; set only what you want to change.
# NOTHING here is a secret — the agent never handles your ChatGPT credentials
# (you log into the dedicated Chrome once, by hand). Do NOT put API keys here.

# --- ChatGPT target ----------------------------------------------------------
# URL a fresh consult opens. Point this at YOUR ChatGPT project to keep every
# consult grouped in one place (recommended). Leave unset for a plain new chat.
#   Find it: open your project in ChatGPT, copy the URL, keep the /project suffix.
# CGC_PROJECT_URL="https://chatgpt.com/g/g-p-<id>-<slug>/project"
#
# Easiest way — no .env / shell rc needed: persist it with the CLI, which stores it
# in the tool's own config (~/.config/cgc/config) that every consult reads:
#   cgc set-project "https://chatgpt.com/g/g-p-<id>-<slug>/project"
#   cgc set-project --clear     # back to a plain new chat
# A CGC_PROJECT_URL env var (below / in your shell) still overrides the stored value.

# Auto model-selection toggle. ON (default): before sending, pick CGC_MODEL in the
# composer and fail closed if it can't be selected — so a consult never silently
# runs on a weaker model. OFF: don't touch the picker, send on whatever is shown.
# CGC_AUTO_MODEL=1        # 1/0 (or true/false, on/off)

# Which tier auto-select targets (only used when CGC_AUTO_MODEL is on). A "Pro*"
# target matches any Pro tier ChatGPT offers (Pro / Pro Extended); never Instant/
# Medium. This is where you spend your ChatGPT Pro subscription — set the strongest
# tier your plan includes.
# CGC_MODEL="Pro"

# --- dedicated debug Chrome --------------------------------------------------
# Remote-debugging port for the dedicated Chrome profile (must be free).
# CGC_PORT=9333

# Where the dedicated Chrome profile lives (kept separate from your normal Chrome;
# CDP is disallowed on the default profile since Chrome 136).
# CGC_PROFILE="$HOME/.cgc-chrome"

# Explicit browser binary. Auto-detected across Chrome/Chromium/Edge on
# macOS + Linux; set this only if detection fails or you want a specific one.
# CGC_CHROME="/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome"

# --- local scratch -----------------------------------------------------------
# TOOL-OWNED scratch for temporary prompt/refs/state files — treat anything here as
# disposable; the tool may clean this path (e.g. `rm -rf`) without warning. If you
# want to KEEP an answer, save it to a separate durable path, e.g. ./cgc_answers/,
# not this directory.
# CGC_STATE_DIR="/tmp/cgc"

# --- egress daemon (auto mode) -----------------------------------------------
# Spool dir for the enqueue/await/watch daemon path (pending/processing/done job
# files + a daemon heartbeat). Needed so `cgc enqueue`/`cgc await` (local-only,
# agent-safe) can hand off to `cgc watch` (the user-started daemon that actually
# talks to chatgpt.com). Same tool-owned-scratch rules as CGC_STATE_DIR.
# CGC_SPOOL_DIR="$CGC_STATE_DIR/spool"

# Let the daemon's egress gate accept gist links. Default off: a gist's visibility
# can't be cheaply proven public the way a repo can via `gh`. Set to 1 only if you
# deliberately intend to deliver via gist.
# CGC_GATE_ALLOW_GIST=0
